# self-check report (regenerated by `make check`)
*_check_report.txt

# maintainer/owner tooling — kept locally, never shipped to participating teams
maintainer/

# Reference microdata you download yourself. NOT redistributable: ANES and GSS
# licences let you use the files, not republish them — and a Zenodo release is
# publication. Keep them here, cite them in registration.md, ship neither.
data/

# Intermediate simulation output, NOT tracked. profiles.csv and
# responses_raw.csv are reproducible from the scripts plus the ANES file; the
# raw model logs in pipeline/out/logs/ are not, and registration K.2 requires
# them for Tier 1 — but they are far too large for git: 45 MB for the
# 850-respondent pilot, so roughly 500 MB at 9,900, against a repository that
# is otherwise well under a megabyte.
#
# K.2 anticipates exactly this: "oversized logs may be a separate linked Zenodo
# upload". So the logs ship as their own Zenodo record, linked from
# registration.md K.2 — they must ship somehow, they just must not ship here.
# Check the actual size after the run with:  du -sh pipeline/out/logs
pipeline/out/

# Credentials. ellmer reads the provider key from the environment
# (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY), so a project-level .Renviron is the
# obvious place to put it — and the obvious way to commit it by accident.
# Keys belong in ~/.Renviron; these patterns are the safety net.
.Renviron
.Renviron.*
.env
.env.*
!.Renviron.example
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# R / editor / OS cruft
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store
